If the table does not exist, you will receive an error message stating the table does not exist.

## Table DROP Command

To drop a table in PostgreSQL, you must execute `DROP TABLE <table_name>;` followed by `;`. If the table has constraints (like `PRIMARY KEY`), you must drop the entire constraint chain before dropping the table. Example:

```sql
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS users;
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS messages;
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS contacts;
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS orders;
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS products;
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS categories;
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS tags;
```

**Note:** If the table has foreign keys pointing to other tables, you must also drop those references. Otherwise, you may not be dropping the underlying data structure correctly.

